jsona — License Overview
==========================

This repository uses a multi-license structure. Different parts of the project
are released under different licenses, summarized below.

| Path              | Component                              | License           |
|-------------------|----------------------------------------|-------------------|
| `packages/core`   | `jsona-core` — parse / serialize / graph / diff (zero-dep) | MIT        |
| `packages/cli`    | `jsona-view` — the `jsona` CLI (query/format/minify/sort/diff/mcp/serve) | MIT |
| `packages/web`    | Web viewer (React + Vite, fully offline-capable) | GPL-3.0-or-later |
| `server/`         | Optional share / sync backend (Node + SQLite) | Proprietary / closed-source |

The full text of each license is available at:
- MIT:        https://opensource.org/license/mit
- GPL-3.0:    https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html
- Proprietary (server/): see `server/LICENSE`

Licensing inquiries for the server backend, or to discuss running it under
different terms, are welcome — contact the jsona team.

---

Open-core model:
The core engine (CLI + libraries) is MIT-licensed so developers can audit,
self-host, and reuse it freely. The web viewer is GPL-3.0 so derivative web
products also stay open. The optional share/sync server is closed-source and is
offered both as a self-hostable component and as a hosted online service — you
can use the fully open parts without depending on it at all.
